    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45753" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑφθημῐμερής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>containing seven
			halves</i>, i.e. <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>: esp. in metre, -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μερές, τό</span>, <i>a measure of three
				feet and a half</i>, such as the first <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i> feet of a Hexameter or Iambic Trimeter, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				7.3
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				302
			</span></i> (pl.), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. τομή</span> a
			caesura after such a phrase, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				1.25
			</span></i>.</div>
